---
import Exp from './Exp.astro';
---

<section id="features">
  <p class="section-label">Features</p>
  <h2>What you get.</h2>
  <div class="does-grid">
    <div class="does-card">
      <svg class="card-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
      <h3>Container sandbox</h3>
      <p>Every <code>devcell &lt;agent&gt;</code> runs inside an isolated cell. SSH keys, other repos, and host credentials are unreachable. The container is the guardrail, not the approval loop.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="does-card">
      <svg class="card-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18.36 6.64a9 9 0 1 1-12.73 0"/><line x1="12" y1="2" x2="12" y2="12"/></svg>
      <h3>Egress lockdown</h3>
      <p><code>devcell claude --solitary</code> denies all outbound traffic except allow-listed domains. The agent cannot phone home, push to the wrong remote, or exfiltrate tokens.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="does-card">
      <svg class="card-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
      <h3>No account, no login</h3>
      <p><code>brew install devcell-sh/tap/devcell</code>, <code>cd your-project</code>, <code>devcell claude</code>. No Docker Hub login, no cloud dashboard, no API key required with Claude Max/Pro.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="does-card">
      <svg class="card-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 0 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 0 1-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 0 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.68 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 0 1 0-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 0 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 4.68a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 0 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 0 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 19.4 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"/></svg>
      <h3>MCP servers with backing tools</h3>
      <p>You don't install MCP servers; they come ready. The backing tools ship too: the agent can run <code>tofu plan</code> or edit PCBs because OpenTofu and KiCad are installed, not just their MCP servers. 11 servers, each pinned to a commit hash.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="does-card">
      <svg class="card-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4"/></svg>
      <h3>Three OS engines</h3>
      <p>Linux container (Docker), macOS VM (Tart), Windows VM (winkit)<Exp name="engine-windows" />. Same commands, same config. Pick the guest with <code>--os</code> and the engine follows.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="does-card">
      <svg class="card-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg>
      <h3>Your config carries over</h3>
      <p>CLAUDE.md, hooks, skills, and MCP config mount into the cell. Your project-level setup works unchanged. 1Password secrets inject at runtime on a RAM-only tmpfs, gone when the cell stops.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="stacks-grid" style="margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
    <div class="stack-row">
      <span class="stack-cat">Project</span>
      <span class="stack-tools">The agent sees the project dir it was launched in. Other repos aren't hidden, they're absent.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack-row">
      <span class="stack-cat">Cell</span>
      <span class="stack-tools">Its own home: dotfiles, shell history, agent memory. Shared across that cell's projects, invisible to other cells.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack-row">
      <span class="stack-cat">Host</span>
      <span class="stack-tools">Nothing outside the mount and the cell home. <code>~/.ssh</code>, <code>~/.aws</code>, your real home: unreachable.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="stacks-more">Docker by default. When your threat model demands a real kernel boundary, <code>--engine tart</code> runs the same cell in a VM.</p>
</section>
